  "maldives": {
    name: "Coco",
    photoKw: "cat,maldives,beach",
    title: "Coco and the Great Sandbank Rescue",
    pages: [
      "Coco was a sandy-cream cat who lived at Kandima, a resort on a tiny island in the Maldives. Her favourite place was the wooden walkway out to the overwater villas, built on stilts right above the lagoon. She would flatten herself on the warm planks and peer down through the gaps. Parrotfish in rainbow colours zoomed past, and once a stingray glided by like a flying carpet.",
      "Every day Coco watched the seaplanes land in a sparkling spray and wondered about the wide blue world beyond her island. She was the resort’s official “welcome cat,” bumping noses with each new family. But Coco had a tiny secret worry: she had never, ever been off her little island, and a small brave part of her wished she could see what lay across the lagoon.",
      "One sunny afternoon a speedboat purred up to the jetty, loaded with picnic baskets for a trip to the sandbank. Quick as a whisker, Coco tiptoed aboard and hid behind a cool-box. The boat zoomed off, bouncing over the waves, and soon arrived at a tiny island of pure white sand — no trees at all, just sea sparkling in every direction. Coco had her adventure at last!",
      "The family spread their picnic blanket while spinner dolphins leaped far out across the water. Coco patrolled her whole new kingdom in about twenty proud steps. Then trouble swooped in: a cheeky seabird dived down to steal a sandwich, snatching it right off the plate! The children gasped. Someone had to do something, and the only hero on the sandbank had four paws and a twitching tail.",
      "Coco puffed up like a fluffy balloon and let out one enormous “MEOWWW!” The startled seabird dropped the sandwich and flapped away over the lagoon. The family cheered and named her the bravest cat in the Maldives. As the sun sank low, they motored back past the house reef, where a green sea turtle surfaced and blew a sleepy “pfft” hello.",
      "Back at Kandima the children begged to take Coco on the giant waterslide to celebrate. She climbed up, peeked over the slippery blue edge at the splashing far below, and decided, very firmly, that sliding was for humans. Hero cats do their heroics on dry land. She found a comfy sun-lounger at the Kandiland kids’ club instead and supervised all the splashing.",
      "That night Coco curled on the warm planks of her favourite walkway, watching the lagoon glow faintly blue with tiny glowing plankton. She had crossed the sea, met the dolphins, saved a sandwich and become a hero — and still come safely home. “The best adventure,” she purred, tucking her nose under her paw, “always ends back where you belong.” And the parrotfish below seemed to agree."
    ]
  },
  "rabat": {
    name: "Zellij",
    photoKw: "cat,morocco,kasbah",
    title: "Zellij and the Blue-and-White Maze",
    pages: [
      "Zellij was a stripy little cat who lived in the Kasbah of the Udayas, a clifftop fort in Rabat where every wall and lane is painted blue and white, the colour of the sky and the sea. Each morning he wove between pots of pink geraniums down to the Andalusian gardens, napped under the orange trees, then climbed the old fort wall to watch the boats on the Bouregreg river. Life was perfect — until the day he chased a bumblebee.",
      "The fat, fuzzy bumblebee bumbled down a twisty alley, and Zellij could not resist. He turned left, turned right, scampered up a ramp and round a corner — and suddenly stopped. Every wall was the same shade of sky-blue! Every doorway looked the same! Zellij sat down with a wobbly little “mew.” For the first time ever, the clever cat of the kasbah was hopelessly, dizzyingly lost in the blue-and-white maze.",
      "He padded this way and that, his tummy starting to rumble. He sniffed cinnamon and leather drifting up from the medina souk, and heard the blue tram dinging far away across the river. But none of it pointed home. Then a sea breeze tickled his whiskers, salty and cool. Zellij lifted his pink nose high and remembered: the great Atlantic Ocean always lay below the kasbah. Follow the breeze, find the sea, find home!",
      "Nose to the wind, Zellij wound through the lanes — and burst out onto the high fort wall just as the sun was sinking. Below him the Atlantic waves rolled gold and silver, and across the water rose the tall stone Hassan Tower among its rows of broken columns. He knew exactly where he was now. But the path home was steep and the light was fading fast.",
      "Carefully, paw over paw, Zellij climbed down toward the gardens. A kind tea-seller spotted the little lost cat and crouched with a saucer of warm goat’s milk. Zellij lapped it gratefully, then trotted ahead, leading the man through the lanes he suddenly knew by heart, past the geraniums, all the way to his own blue doorway.",
      "The tea-seller laughed, poured himself a glass of frothy mint tea, and gave Zellij a gentle scratch behind the ears. Storks clacked goodnight from the towers of nearby Chellah, where they nest among the old Roman ruins. Zellij curled up on a warm tiled step, full of milk and very pleased with himself.",
      "From then on, whenever Zellij felt the salty breeze, he remembered his lesson: even in the bluest, twistiest maze, the sea will always show you the way home. He still chased the occasional bumblebee, of course — but only the slow ones, and never, ever round more than one corner. And every evening he watched Rabat turn gold, the proudest little cat in all of Morocco."
    ]
  },
  "lapland": {
    name: "Lumi",
    photoKw: "cat,snow,white",
    title: "Lumi and the Night the Sky Lit Up",
    pages: [
      "Lumi was a fluffy snow-white cat who lived at Santa Claus Village in Rovaniemi, right on the Arctic Circle line where you can stand in two places at once. She loved to hide in the elves’ post office, batting at the thousands of letters waiting for Santa. Outside, the snow squeaked and the reindeer jingled, and Lumi was so white that, sitting still, she nearly vanished.",
      "One snowy evening the head elf hurried in, very worried. A whole sack of children’s letters had blown out into the dark forest, and the elves were too busy wrapping presents to search. “Whoever shall find them in all this snow?” he sighed. Lumi’s ears pricked up. A white cat, in white snow, who could see in the dark — this was a job made just for her.",
      "Lumi slipped out past the husky kennels, where the dogs were harnessed for their evening run. She trotted alongside the swishing sled into the silent, snowy forest, her paws making the tiniest prints. But the wind had scattered the letters far and wide, tucking them under frosty branches and into drifts. The night grew darker and colder, and Lumi began to fear she would never find them all.",
      "Then she looked up — and gasped. The whole sky had begun to glow and swirl in ribbons of green and violet: the Northern Lights! The shimmering light spilled down over the snow, and there, glittering in its glow, lay letter after letter after letter, scattered like white stars. Lumi could see every single one. She gathered them gently in her mouth, two and three at a time.",
      "By the time the lights faded, Lumi had carried every last letter back to the warm post office. The elves cheered and the head elf gave her a tiny medal of icicle-silver. Lumi swished her tail, secretly certain she had switched the great lights on herself. Then she curled up against a sleepy reindeer, purring, the cosiest cat on the whole Arctic Circle — and dreamed of swirling green skies until morning."
    ]
  },
